# CODEOWNERS — out-of-repo checklist A4.
#
# Sole founder today, so this is @acarpcreate on everything and changes nothing about
# who reviews what. The value is structural: it makes review non-optional later, when
# it is no longer just you, without anyone having to remember to set it up. It also
# gives GitHub something to attach "require review from Code Owners" to in branch
# protection.
#
# Ownership is only enforced if branch protection on `main` has "Require a pull request
# before merging" plus "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. This file alone does
# nothing — same class of gap as the can_deliver revoke that never applied.

# Everything, by default.
*                           @acarpcreate

# --- Tier-3 surfaces: called out so they are visibly owned rather than covered by the
# --- wildcard. When a second reviewer exists, these are the paths where a second pair
# --- of eyes matters most, per the audit findings.

# Schema and authorization. RLS is the authorization layer; every table ships with
# policies, and a permission change here is the one that can silently widen access.
/supabase/migrations/       @acarpcreate
/supabase/tests/            @acarpcreate

# The security harnesses. If these are weakened, the CI gate stops proving anything —
# and three of the four self-corrections across the audit were harness bugs that made
# results look cleaner than they were.
/scripts/security/          @acarpcreate

# CI and repo automation. The gate itself.
/.github/                   @acarpcreate

# Service-role call sites. Six of the seven sit on unauthenticated, publicly reachable
# paths (audit row B6); a bug in any one of them is an RLS bypass rather than a 403.
/src/lib/supabase/admin.ts  @acarpcreate
/src/app/api/portal/        @acarpcreate
/src/app/api/stripe/        @acarpcreate

# Auth gate and its exemption list.
/src/middleware.ts          @acarpcreate
/src/lib/supabase/middleware.ts @acarpcreate

# Money and rights logic.
/src/lib/stripe/            @acarpcreate
/src/lib/agreements.ts      @acarpcreate
